The fresh name conservatively avoids every known identifier, including free references; the final link comparison catches changes due to other new parsing rules. Preserving names and bindings alone cannot establish equivalence if the new edition also changes arithmetic or evaluation order, so run relevant behavior tests too. This workflow is a design example, not a claim about every edition migration tool.
